    <div class="sec-head"><span class="eyebrow">Good to know</span><h2 id="q-h">Questions we often get</h2></div>
    <div class="faq">
      <details><summary>When should I book safari permits?</summary><p>As early as possible. Core-zone permits for popular parks like Tadoba open months ahead and morning slots in peak season sell out quickly. Send us your dates and we'll check availability before you commit.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Is a tiger sighting guaranteed?</summary><p>No one can promise that, and we won't. What we do is choose the right zones, seasons and number of safaris to give you the best realistic chance, along with everything else the forest has to offer: leopards, sloth bears, gaur, wild dogs and hundreds of bird species.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What's the difference between core and buffer zones?</summary><p>Core zones are the protected heart of the reserve and usually have the most sightings. Buffer zones surround the core, are less crowded and often stay open during the monsoon. A good plan usually mixes both.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can you plan trips for families and first-timers?</summary><p>Yes. We pick comfortable stays, sensible safari timings and naturalists who are great with children and new visitors, so the trip is relaxed and rewarding.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What's included in a package?</summary><p>Typically stays, meals, safari permits, gypsy and guide, and naturalist support. Transfers from Nagpur or Amravati can be added. Your quote lists exactly what is and isn't included.</p></details>
